  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-19T22:21:14.773Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "[Before starting with the rant, I admit that I don't know if this is a problem that accours on other vr platforms other than the Quest 2]\nThis is how I feel when writing/editing a previousely written bio. \nYou can't scroll through it. You can't edit a specific portion of it; so if you notice a word at the beginning or in the middle of your bio, you have to delete EVERYTHING in front of that word, before actually making the adjustments that you think are fit. \nI propose that a new way of entering text in VRChat is introduced, that has all the quality of life features mentioned above built into it. So, without even mentioning everything that could be done, I say that implementing the Quest 2 internal keybord would be the best option for Quest users. Lastly, for the other platforms I believe that a new keybord should be built from the ground up.",
